+## 4. Highest-ROI remaining work (ordered by expected-gain × breadth ÷ cost)
+
+### 4.1 `many_syms`: close the 2.4× gap to wild — **biggest single win**
+
+Callgrind attribution after this session's fixes (20k-symbol link, 53.7M Ir):
+
+| Cost | Share | Note |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `_int_malloc` + `free` + `malloc_consolidate` + `_int_free_chunk` | **~22%** | `String` per symbol |
+| symtab sort (`partition_lomuto` + `insert_tail`) | ~13% | after the u128 fix |
+| `emit_executable` body | ~10% | |
+| `memcpy` | ~7.6% | `section_data` `to_vec()` |
+| `HashMap::insert` + `get_mut` | ~9.6% | `String` keys |
+| `read_cstr` + `from_utf8` | ~8.7% | one `String` per name |
+
+**The dominant cost is one heap allocation per symbol name.** Two changes,
+in dependency order:
+
+1. **Symbol interning (`SymbolId(u32)`).** Intern every name once into a single
+   arena; replace `FxHashMap<String, GlobalSymbol>` with
+   `FxHashMap<SymbolId, GlobalSymbol>`. Removes the malloc traffic *and* the
+   string hashing/compare in the hot maps. Expected **−25–35%** instructions on
+   symbol-heavy links. Estimated 1–1.5 days; touches `linker_common/symbols.rs`,
+   `types.rs`, `dynamic.rs`, all four backends. Do this **first** — several
+   items below get easier once names are `Copy`.
+2. **Borrowed section data / mmap input.** `parse_elf64_object` copies every
+   section with `to_vec()` after `std::fs::read` already copied the file. An
+   arena/lifetime model (or `mmap`) removes the largest single memcpy.
+   Expected −20–30% on large links. Dependency policy: prefer a small `unsafe`
+   `mmap` wrapper over adding `memmap2`.
+
+### 4.2 Wire the parallel store path into `emit_exec`
+
+`parallel_reloc.rs` is now **sound and well-tested but still unused** —
+`emit_exec` writes relocations inline. Wiring requires splitting the reloc loop
+into (a) resolution, which mutates instruction bytes for TLS/GOTPCRELX
+relaxation and must stay serial, and (b) a pure `RelocWrite` list. Expected
+1.3–1.8× on reloc-heavy links at ≥4 cores; **no gain on this 2-core VM**, which
+is why it was not attempted here — measure on the 14700KF.
+
+### 4.3 ICF apply
+
+`icf.rs` analyses and classifies but never folds. Applying it needs symbol and
+relocation redirection plus dropping folded sections. This is the main
+remaining *size* lever against wild.
+
+### 4.4 Remaining feature gaps
+
+`--version-script` on ET_EXEC · positional `--as-needed` · `--exclude-libs` ·
+`--emit-relocs` (also unlocks `CONFIG_RELOCATABLE` kernels) · ELF32 script path
+(`setup.elf`) · `--print-map` as an alias for `-Map=/dev/stdout`.
+
+### 4.5 Fuzzing depth
+
+The current fuzzer is a byte mutator over 4 seeds. Next: a *grammar-aware* ELF
+generator (valid-but-hostile structures: overlapping sections, cyclic
+`sh_link`, 0-size `SHT_GROUP`, INCLUDE cycles in scripts) and `cargo-fuzz`
+targets for `parse_elf64_object`, `parse_archive_members` and
+`parse_linker_script`. Also fuzz the **archive** and **linker-script** seeds
+harder — this session's campaign was dominated by `.o` mutants.
+
+### 4.6 Structural debt
+
+* `emit_exec.rs` is ~1900 lines with layout, symtab, relocation and header
+  emission interleaved; `layout_plan.rs` exists but is **still not wired**.
+  The `vaddr!`/`new_segment!` macros added this session are a local fix — the
+  real cleanup is to make `LayoutPlan` own segment assignment.
+* **`emit_script.rs` still has the page-padding defect.** `emit_exec.rs` and
+  `emit_shared.rs` were both fixed this session; the script path (kernel
+  links, `-T`) was not, because its addresses come from the script's own
+  `SECTIONS`/`. =` assignments and the fix is not a mechanical copy — the
+  bias must be derived from the script-assigned vaddr rather than imposed.
+  **This is the top structural item**: three near-duplicate layout engines is
+  why one fix needed applying twice and still is not complete. Unify them
+  behind `LayoutPlan` (which exists and is still unwired) instead of porting
+  the fix a third time.
+* `link_shared`'s hand-written argument parser still duplicates `args.rs` and
+  therefore misses `-Map=` and every bug fixed there.
